From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GBrain Ops <person@example.test>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:09:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ingestion): log owner embedding failures

The owner's embedding loop caught every pass failure, recorded a generic
health string, and retried with backoff without logging. A
misconfigured embedding provider therefore stopped all embedding with
nothing in the owner logs.

Warn when a failure streak starts and at most hourly while it lasts.
Name the model signature and the error class plus structured
credential-preflight fields, never the error message, which can carry
provider responses or page content. A stale remainder warns only after
it survives several retries, since writes landing mid-pass routinely
leave a short-lived one. Log recovery once the streak ends.
